Subject: [PATCH] desktop: add "Restart Kodi" to the Estuary power menu

RestartApp ends Kodi with exit code 65. On LibreELEC systemd starts Kodi
again; kodi-standalone treats 65 as a clean exit, so Kodi only closes.
Start Kodi again on 65 in kodi-standalone, and add the item after Exit.

--- a/tools/Linux/kodi-standalone.sh.in
+++ b/tools/Linux/kodi-standalone.sh.in
@@ -35,7 +35,10 @@
   $APP
   RET=$?
   NOW=$(date +%s)
-  if [ $RET -ge 64 ] && [ $RET -le 66 ] || [ $RET -eq 0 ]; then # clean exit
+  if [ $RET -eq 65 ]; then # RestartApp: start again
+    LASTSUCCESSFULSTART=$NOW
+    CRASHCOUNT=0
+  elif [ $RET -ge 64 ] && [ $RET -le 66 ] || [ $RET -eq 0 ]; then # clean exit
     LOOP=0
   else # crash
     DIFF=$((NOW-LASTSUCCESSFULSTART))
--- a/addons/skin.estuary/xml/DialogButtonMenu.xml
+++ b/addons/skin.estuary/xml/DialogButtonMenu.xml
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@
 						<visible>System.ShowExitButton</visible>
 					</item>
 					<item>
+						<label>$LOCALIZE[13313] Kodi</label>
+						<onclick>RestartApp</onclick>
+					</item>
+					<item>
 						<label>$LOCALIZE[13016]</label>
 						<onclick>Powerdown()</onclick>
 						<visible>System.CanPowerDown</visible>
